    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Kobolds are small, loud, enthusiastic, and devoted to their warrens, their friends, and any dragon that will have them, which makes them some of the Fenari's favorite hosts. A caravan that stumbles into a Kobold warren is usually adopted within the week.</p><p>Kobold Fenari shrink over the generations and grow a little scaly around the edges, though they keep their fur and their bite. They pick up the Kobold talent for fighting as a pack: alone, a Kobold Fenari is a nuisance; in a group, they're an avalanche of tiny teeth and piercing yips.</p><p>Their loyalty is legendary. A Kobold Fenari who calls you a friend will follow you into a dragon's lair, probably while asking whether the dragon is friendly, and whether it might like to meet them. They tend toward lawful neutral.</p><p><strong>Size.</strong> Living among Kobolds has made these Fenari smaller than their kin, most growing between 2'10\" and 3'6\" tall and weighing 30 to 50 pounds. Your size is Small.</p><p><strong>Languages.</strong> Most Kobold Fenari learn Draconic.</p><h3>Kobold Culture Traits</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Level</th><th>Traits</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Rally Yip</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Unison Strike</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Pack Pounce</td></tr></tbody></table>",
      "chat": ""
    },
